{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/60354-pets-and-pacts","id":60354,"title":"Pets and Pacts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-28T19:57:11-08:00","id":60354,"title":"Pets and Pacts","content":"One of my players likes to hang around pet hospitals and poach pacts from desperate pet owners.<br /> <br /> She also is exploring the option of helping people find lost pets.<br /> <br /> What are the limits of a pact in this regard?<br /> <br /> What kind of benefit would 'find my lost pet' be?<br /> <br /> Would it work if the pet had come to some sort of nefarious end? Would it 'replace' them?<br /> <br /> Or is a pet considered a separate soul?<br /> <br /> Can you make a pact to remove a condition from your pet, or would your pet have to somehow consent to that pact itself, making it impossible?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T09:42:05-08:00","id":60849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/60354-pets-and-pacts#post60354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What kind of benefit would 'find my lost pet' be?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say a +1 level, since you're essentially giving them a 1-dot Retainer and it requires altering the world outside of the Pact-signer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/60354-pets-and-pacts#post60354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would it work if the pet had come to some sort of nefarious end? Would it 'replace' them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Two options here. First, it connects the Pact-signer with a similar-enough pet and modifies the Pact-signer's memories so that the similar-enough pet IS the lost pet for all intents and purposes. Second, see: Resurrection. Also: Rule #2.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/60354-pets-and-pacts#post60354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or is a pet considered a separate soul?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but I'm not sure how that applies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/60354-pets-and-pacts#post60354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you make a pact to remove a condition from your pet, or would your pet have to somehow consent to that pact itself, making it impossible?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah. I see no reason you cannot create a Pact to benefit another, though by definition you'll be &quot;affecting another&quot;, meaning it'll be the more costly of the listed benefits. So no, your pet would not have to consent if you made a Pact with the owner.<br /> <br /> HOWEVER!!<br /> <br /> Something to remember:<br /> <br /> Animals have languages of their own. Dolphins have been recorded to use vocalizations to communicate, with unique identifiers for each other. Pack animals certainly communicate with each other. Chimpanzees vocalize as part of their hunting as a troop.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demon the Descent, page 183</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">System: Demons gain the Eidetic Memory Merit(p. 288)at character creation. In addition, <b>all of the Unchained are fluent in every native human language currently in use.</b> This includes local dialects as well as slang and innuendo \u2014 the demon can speak any language like a native speaker.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, it specifies <b>human</b> languages, but not all Angels are sent as humans! Some are animals, some are buildings, some are completely non-humanoid life forms. Additionally, some Angels would be equipped to speak to and influence animals as part of their Mission. I'd stipulate that being seen to actually converse with animals (and have them respond intelligently as opposed to just talking to them) might be a Cover Compromise (unless you're Cesar Millan). At minimum, I don't see any reason any Demon should be prohibited from having a Modification or an Embed that would allow them to converse with animals.<br /> <br /> Also: Rule #2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Once is happenstance. Twice is coincidence. Three times is enemy action. Four times is Infrastructure.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> Rule #2: Never let the game-mechanics get in the way of a good story.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1642-paddon","name":"Paddon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1642_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}